WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.367
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This "Late Night."

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.834
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.234
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:08.000
President Biden reportedly
told aides in a recent meeting

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.300
that they need
to make progress

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.567
in reversing his decline
in poll numbers.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:14.400
And hopefully Jill and Travis
will understand.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:18.901
According to a new report,

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.334
President Biden frequently
tells aides and friends

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.367
in private conversations
that he feels

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.167
"so much younger than his age."

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.334
And I'm sure he does,

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.767
but it doesn't inspire
a ton of confidence

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:33.033
when you walk around
saying, "Man, I feel 73!"

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.801
According to a new report,
First Lady Dr. Jill Biden

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.701
is trying to improve
President Biden's diet,

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:42.501
or at least trying to get him
to add another food group.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:45.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.667
The two Georgia
election workers

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:52.033
who won $148 million verdict
on Friday against Rudy Giuliani

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.234
filed another lawsuit yesterday
after Giuliani

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.334
continued making false
statements about them.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:01.667
Only Rudy could lose
a $148 million lawsuit

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.200
and say, [As Giuliani]
"Alright, double or nothing!

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.234
Put it all on blue!"

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.234
A new poll found
that 3 in 10 people

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.100
who voted for
former President Trump

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.901
want a president who is
willing to break rules and laws.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.968
And in an act of desperation,

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.267
Biden ripped the tags
off his mattress.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.434
According to a new poll,

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.200
Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.300
has an approval rating
of just 6%.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.501
Incidentally, 6% is also
what he's buffering at.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:35.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.267
In a new campaign ad,

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.167
Republican presidential hopeful
Nikki Haley

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.434
says that President Biden
is too old

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.300
and calls for term limits
and mental competency tests,

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:51.400
which is why we need young,
sharp politicians

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.234
like New York Mayor Eric Adams.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.334
-When you look at
the totality of the year,

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:56.434
if you had to describe it,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:57.934
and it's tough to do,
in one word,

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.300
what would that word be,
and tell me why?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.601
-New York.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:05.133
This is a place
where every day you wake up,

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.834
you could experience
everything from a plane

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:11.534
crashing into our Trade Center
to a person

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.934
who's celebrating
a new business that's opened.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.300
This is a very,
very complicated city,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.567
and that's why it's
the greatest city on the globe.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:30.567
-Honey!

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.067
I don't want to go
to New York anymore!

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.167
Nikki Haley is right.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.400
Term limits might be
a good idea.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.400
How about half a term?
Is that too soon?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.234
Georgia Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:44.200
over the weekend
met Jacob Chansley,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.968
the so-called QAnon shaman,
in what is being called

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.501
Hallmark's
worst Christmas movie ever.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:56.501
The Greek yogurt company Chobani
has acquired the coffee chain

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.000
La Colombe for $900 million

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.801
because they are dedicated
to making sure

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.868
their customers [laughs]
never leave the bathroom.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:08.767
You know, finally, a man
in Alabama

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.801
who was arrested recently
for alleged possession

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.868
of a controlled substance
had a parrot on his shoulder

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.534
and told officers he was high
on mushrooms.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:19.067
Said the parrot, [as parrot]
"Don't forget the crack!"

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.667
Not good. Not good. We --

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:27.467
In rehearsal, I nail--
Oh, the parrot was good earlier.

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.868
I shouldn't have burned it when
we were doing cards earlier.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:32.868
[ Imitating parrot ]

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.834
No, I still don't have it.

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.467
Maybe later in the show,
we'll get back to it.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.901
That was a monologue, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:42.300
We've got a great show
for you tonight.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.300
She is an Emmy-winning
writer, comedian, and actress

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.934
from my home state
of New Hampshire --

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.300
hometown even, Bedford.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.734
You can see her in the
critically acclaimed "Maestro,"

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.400
which is in theaters now
and on Netflix tomorrow.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.133
The wonderful,
one of our favorites,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.734
Sarah Silverman,
is back on the show, everybody.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.567
-And you know her

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.267
from "Russian Doll"
and "The Morning Show."

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.767
She stars in one of my favorite
movies of the year,

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:05.801
"Past Lives."

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.133
It's beautiful, it's wonderful.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:11.467
Greta Lee will also be
joining us,

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.901
and he is
a James Beard Award-winning chef

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:17.734
whose book "Mi Cocina:
Recipes and Rapture

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:19.534
From My Kitchen in Mexico"
is available now.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.567
We will be cooking with chef
Rick Martinez, everybody.

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:24.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.734
Hey, you guys, my brother and I,

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.501
we have a podcast called
"Family Trips."

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.601
We talk to people
about the family trips

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:31.968
they took when they were kids.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:34.100
We have a great episode
this week with Nate Bargatze.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.901
He is fantastic, as always.
Do check that out.

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:39.601
Also, if you are in Las Vegas
on New Year's Eve

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.334
and you are looking
for something to do,

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:43.167
me and my friend John Oliver

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:46.334
will be at the Colosseum
at Caesars Palace in Las Vegas.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.400
Come check us out.
We are so happy.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.934
We're so excited
to do that show

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.968
and then as soon as it's over,
go right to bed.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:57.734
That is how John and I party,
you guys.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.601
Uh, moving on, this morning
I was practicing

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:02.834
my hockey stops in the
Rockefeller ice skating rink

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:06.767
when I overheard
a family of Austrian tourists

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.367
discussing a new breed
of migrating tree frogs, and --

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.300
[ Sniffing ]
Wait. I am so sorry.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.734
I could be wrong here,
but I think I smell some smoke

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.000
and that can only mean
one thing.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.434
It's time for "Ya Burnt."

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:24.167
♪♪

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:25.601
Welcome to the Burn Zone.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:28.100
We got a lot of topics to sizzle
through and not a lot of time.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.167
Over here is the burner.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.234
Let's turn on the gas
and load her up.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:34.367
Whoo! Feliz navidadi!

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.434
First up, ornaments.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:43.434
Hey, ornaments, if I wanted
to see dusty red balls

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.367
hanging under a shaggy thicket,

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:48.133
I'd go to the YMCA
on a weekday afternoon.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:49.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:51.501
That's right. We're starting
with a testicles joke.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:54.200
That's how we do Christmas
in Burn Town.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.400
Hey, ornaments,
you know what I don't want

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.367
dangling precariously off a twig

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.367
in a house
with three kids and a dog?

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.567
Something that shatters.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.033
You want me to hang orbs

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.667
of the world's thinnest glass
at toddler eye level?

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.467
Why don't I just
paint the word "noel"

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.133
on some hand grenades instead?

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.501
Also, it's bad enough
we just ripped

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:13.901
a healthy young tree
out of the ground.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.400
Now we got to desecrate
the corpse

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.601
by dressing it up like
a stripper at a bachelor party?

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:21.167
It's bringing holiday cheer,
not starting an OnlyFans.

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:24.033
And not only are the
store-bought ornaments bad,

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.567
now I got to pretend
to be impressed

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:29.234
by those homemade monstrosities
my kids bring home from school?

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:32.067
Wow, you made this
with just popsicle sticks

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.400
and all the glue?

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.534
I...never would have guessed.

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:37.434
Let's hang it in the back
facing the wall

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:38.968
with all your
other masterpieces.

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:40.501
Side burn my infant daughter.

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:43.133
-Side burn!

00:06:43.133 --> 00:06:44.400
-It's okay.
She won't see this.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.868
She only ever
watches the monologue.

00:06:45.868 --> 00:06:47.234
Hey, ornaments!

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:50.801
Time to join the Yule log
in the fireplace, ya burnt!

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.067
Advent calendars.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:53.634
Ah, advent calendars --

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:55.834
the least efficient way
to distribute candy

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:58.200
since Halloween brought us
door-to-door begging.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:01.667
If you want gifts
before Christmas that badly,

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:03.901
do what I did and marry
into a Jewish family.

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:06.567
-Marrying up!

00:07:06.567 --> 00:07:08.601
-The great thing
about advent calendars

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:10.501
is when you give a kid
one piece of candy,

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:13.868
they're totally satisfied
for the next 24 hours.

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:16.267
You ever tried to give a kid
one piece of candy?

00:07:16.267 --> 00:07:19.767
You know what would work better?
24 advent calendars.

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:21.667
And if you're worried
about the candy not being fresh

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:23.501
by the time you open it
on December 24th,

00:07:23.501 --> 00:07:26.133
remember they packed it
in April.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:27.534
Here's an idea,
advent calendars --

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:29.234
make one of you
that counts down the days

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:32.868
to the 2024 election so I really
know when to beg Jesus for help.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:35.634
-Fill it with Xanax!

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:37.133
-Advent calendars,

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:39.100
did I accidentally
hang you over a menorah?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.601
'Cause ya burnt!

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:41.801
Mulled wine.

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:43.067
Finally, an answer
to the question

00:07:43.067 --> 00:07:45.200
what if potpourri
could get you [bleep] up?

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:50.601
Not to play sommelier here,
but I'm pretty sure red wine

00:07:50.601 --> 00:07:53.567
is meant to be served at room
temp or slightly chilled,

00:07:53.567 --> 00:07:56.467
not scalding hot
and full of mulch.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:57.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.801 --> 00:07:59.267
Also, I don't know
if it technically counts

00:07:59.267 --> 00:08:01.067
as a secret family recipe
if you throw in

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.334
a pinch of every single spice
in your pantry.

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:06.968
But at least we finally polished
off the jar of cloves Aunt Judy

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:08.801
gave us when Bush
was still in office.

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:10.901
-Mission accomplished!

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:14.834
-Hey, mulled wine,
mull this over. Ya burnt.

00:08:14.834 --> 00:08:16.200
Caroling.
Oh, good.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.100
Sober karaoke with strangers
is available for delivery.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:23.567
And they do all of the songs
I already have on Spotify,

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:24.834
but worse?

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:26.000
Sign me up.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.767
This is the real
"Nightmare Before Christmas."

00:08:27.767 --> 00:08:30.634
Nothing more disappointing than
thinking your Thai food is here,

00:08:30.634 --> 00:08:33.834
then opening the door to find
your 10 weirdest neighbors

00:08:33.834 --> 00:08:37.601
informing you
Christ the Savior is born.

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:41.334
I want my Pad Thai,
God damn it!

00:08:41.334 --> 00:08:43.701
You're like if Jehovah's
Witnesses went to theatre camp.

00:08:43.701 --> 00:08:46.067
Hey, carolers, how about
you do "Silent Night"?

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:49.000
Not the song, the activity.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.667
So let me make something clear.

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:52.834
I will wish you
a merry Christmas,

00:08:52.834 --> 00:08:55.801
but I will not be bringing you
some figgy pudding.

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.501
I don't have
any figgy pudding.

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.300
I don't know where
to get figgy pudding.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.634
If Whole Foods hasn't figured

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:02.734
out figgy pudding,
then no one has figgy pudding,

00:09:02.734 --> 00:09:05.334
you absolute psychopaths.

00:09:05.334 --> 00:09:07.801
Hey, carolers, go
fa-la-la-la-la-ck yourself.

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:10.434
Ya burnt!

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:12.434
Those commercials
where people get a car

00:09:12.434 --> 00:09:14.701
for Christmas with a big bow
on it, let's cut the [bleep].

00:09:14.701 --> 00:09:16.968
It's never happened.

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:18.868
I don't even believe that people
are giving each other cars

00:09:18.868 --> 00:09:20.934
for Christmas, let alone ones
with big bows on them.

00:09:20.934 --> 00:09:23.434
And if they did,
it would never look like that.

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:25.434
Imagine your dad
in the driveway on Christmas Eve

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:28.267
trying to curl a ribbon
with a giant pair of scissors,

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.200
cursing so loud
the whole neighborhood can hear.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.868
He's not keeping this a secret.

00:09:31.868 --> 00:09:33.534
And let me get this straight --
you're asking about a --

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:35.834
you're asking a fictional
demigod from the North Pole

00:09:35.834 --> 00:09:37.501
to bring you a free vehicle,

00:09:37.501 --> 00:09:40.601
and you opted for a Kia Sorento?

00:09:40.601 --> 00:09:44.367
You don't give a Kia with a bow.
You give it with a gift receipt.

00:09:44.367 --> 00:09:46.634
Hey, giant car bows, this going
to be a December to remember,

00:09:46.634 --> 00:09:48.434
because ya burnt!

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:52.067
Hey, elves! Elves!

00:09:52.067 --> 00:09:53.901
Hey, elves!

00:09:53.901 --> 00:09:55.868
Elves!!

00:09:55.868 --> 00:09:57.834
I'm just going to say it --
you're all getting played.

00:09:57.834 --> 00:09:59.334
You've been working
200-hour work weeks

00:09:59.334 --> 00:10:01.767
with no vacation for, what,
three, four centuries?

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.300
You do all the work
and the credit

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.734
goes to the jolly fat man?

00:10:04.734 --> 00:10:06.133
You're either going
to have to unionize

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:07.868
or take out Santa,
'cause at some point

00:10:07.868 --> 00:10:09.567
enough is enough.

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:11.267
And look, elves,
we're pro-labor here.

00:10:11.267 --> 00:10:12.968
We support you,
but I do not

00:10:12.968 --> 00:10:15.534
and I will never support
Elf on the Shelf.

00:10:15.534 --> 00:10:17.033
All your friends
are doing hard work,

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:18.167
and you're spying on children?

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:21.033
You a creep, bro.

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:22.834
I feel like
they give pervy elves that job

00:10:22.834 --> 00:10:25.133
the same way priests
get moved to a new parish.

00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:27.767
[ Audience groans, laughter ]

00:10:31.767 --> 00:10:33.434
[ Blows ]

00:10:33.434 --> 00:10:36.267
Elves, time to go jump in the
snow, because ya burnt!

00:10:36.267 --> 00:10:39.334
Malls,
the Amazon.com of the '80s.

00:10:39.334 --> 00:10:41.934
Have you been
to a mall recently, kids?

00:10:41.934 --> 00:10:44.567
No? Well, guess what.
You're missing out!

00:10:44.567 --> 00:10:47.534
Gen Z, get off TikTok
and go to the mall.

00:10:47.534 --> 00:10:50.501
And, malls, you make your own
algorithm, man.

00:10:50.501 --> 00:10:52.701
Check these out!

00:10:52.701 --> 00:10:54.167
Did I get these at a store?

00:10:54.167 --> 00:10:56.200
No, bro. I got them at a hut!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:57.501 --> 00:10:58.801
I didn't even
have to pay for them.

00:10:58.801 --> 00:11:01.133
I waited for 15 minutes to see
if anybody worked there,

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:03.834
and when nobody showed up,
I just took them.

00:11:03.834 --> 00:11:05.367
Then I waded around
in the fountain,

00:11:05.367 --> 00:11:07.968
gathered enough quarters to play
"Mortal Kombat" at the arcade

00:11:07.968 --> 00:11:09.267
until my fingers bled.

00:11:09.267 --> 00:11:11.701
Sounds like a full day, right?
Wrong!

00:11:11.701 --> 00:11:14.567
Because then I swooped
over to Lids

00:11:14.567 --> 00:11:17.434
and copped this sweet hat.

00:11:17.434 --> 00:11:22.634
Did a pit stop at Auntie Anne's
for a month's worth of carbs.

00:11:22.634 --> 00:11:24.801
And, look, I know
you can get pornography

00:11:24.801 --> 00:11:27.334
at the tip of your fingers,
blah, blah, blah, blah, blah,

00:11:27.334 --> 00:11:29.167
but you can also pop
into Spencer's Gifts,

00:11:29.167 --> 00:11:30.300
drop by the poster rack,

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.467
and have
a whole-ass relationship

00:11:31.467 --> 00:11:33.133
with a picture
of a bikini-clad model

00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:35.067
sprawled out on the hood
of a Porsche!

00:11:35.067 --> 00:11:36.701
That's living,

00:11:36.701 --> 00:11:38.901
and that's why malls
are this weeks unburnable.

00:11:38.901 --> 00:11:40.434
[ Angelic music plays ]

00:11:40.434 --> 00:11:42.133
Ascend to safety!

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:45.033
[ Applause ]

00:11:46.834 --> 00:11:48.667
How many days ago
did we get these pretzels?

00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:50.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.868 --> 00:11:55.634
Wreaths!

00:11:55.634 --> 00:11:57.267
Oh, look,
it's the Christmas tree's

00:11:57.267 --> 00:12:00.567
crackhead cousin
outside your door again.

00:12:00.567 --> 00:12:02.234
Want to show people
you have a holiday spirit,

00:12:02.234 --> 00:12:03.601
but don't want to put
any effort to it?

00:12:03.601 --> 00:12:05.067
Try a wreath.

00:12:05.067 --> 00:12:07.767
Nothing like paying 50 bucks for
the scraps from the real trees.

00:12:07.767 --> 00:12:11.300
It's like going to a pizza place
and ordering just crust.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:12.801
What's the point
of a wreath anyway?

00:12:12.801 --> 00:12:15.367
Is it a warning
to the other trees?

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:17.601
The only good news
is I can sweep up all that crap

00:12:17.601 --> 00:12:20.200
that falls off my wreath
and use it to make mulled wine.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.267
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.267 --> 00:12:24.167
Hey, wreaths,
I'm rethinking you,

00:12:24.167 --> 00:12:27.133
and I decided ya burnt.

00:12:27.133 --> 00:12:29.000
The Christmas goose.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.133
Oh, no!

00:12:31.133 --> 00:12:34.467
Oh, no! The goose!

00:12:34.467 --> 00:12:36.767
I completely forgot
to take out the goose.

00:12:36.767 --> 00:12:41.701
Oh, no! My beautiful 12-pound
goose that I fattened all year.

00:12:41.701 --> 00:12:45.267
Oh, no. Oh, please be okay,
the goose.

00:12:45.267 --> 00:12:46.234
Please be okay!

00:12:46.234 --> 00:12:48.801
Oh, no.

00:12:48.801 --> 00:12:50.834
Oh.

00:12:50.834 --> 00:12:53.000
Oh, why didn't this part burn?

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.033
[ Laughter ]

00:12:57.234 --> 00:12:58.667
[ Coughs ]

00:13:02.167 --> 00:13:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.801 --> 00:13:05.567
I just realized
I'm still wearing the hat.

00:13:05.567 --> 00:13:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.501 --> 00:13:09.133
Goose, ya burnt!

00:13:09.133 --> 00:13:10.801
Up next, Tiny Tim.

00:13:10.801 --> 00:13:12.400
Listen up,
you Cratchit-y little bitch.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.400
[ Buzzer ]
Oh, that buzzer means

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:15.334
we're out of time.

00:13:15.334 --> 00:13:16.767
Looks like I'll have to

00:13:16.767 --> 00:13:19.100
burn your Dickens off
next one out.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:20.567
This is has been "Ya Burnt."

00:13:20.567 --> 00:13:22.467
We'll be right back
with Sarah Silverman.

